# Platform ratings (ZAPI)

**When:** users rate **people**, **spaces (communities)**, or **arbitrary app entities** (menus, listings, posts) with the same network-wide score the main VTC app uses.

**Not this:** **App Store–style app reviews** (`app_reviews` in ZAPI) — star + text for **published apps** in the marketplace. Do not bolt custom `reviews` / 1–5-star Mongo collections onto entities that should use platform ratings.

**Auth:** `auth-bootstrap.mdc` — ratings require a logged-in user JWT (`?token=` / `posif_token`). Guests may **read** aggregates you expose via your own public API; write endpoints need auth.

**Spec (shell + legacy notes):** `~/apps/app/docs/network-apps-api-spec.md` §K  
**ZAPI implementation:** `~/api/src/zapi/api/routers/ratings.py`, `~/api/src/zapi/services/ratings_service.py`

---

## API (canonical)

Base: **`https://api.vtc.com`** + `/api/v1` (see `env-development.mdc`). Legacy `POST /ratings/addratings` → **`POST /api/v1/ratings`**.

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| `POST` | `/api/v1/ratings` | Add or update the caller’s score |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/ratings/last?to_id=&to_type=` | Caller’s last score for target |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/ratings/summary?to_id=&to_type=` | Aggregate, count, viewer’s last score |

**Body (`POST`):**

| Field | Required | Notes |
|-------|----------|-------|
| `rating` | yes | Integer **−10 … +10** |
| `to_id` | yes | **Numeric string** (community/user id, or app-chosen id for `item`) |
| `to_type` | yes | `user` \| `community` \| `item` |

**Success:** legacy-shaped `{ "status": "success", "result": <aggregate> }` after client unwrap (aggregate is typically shown on a **~1–10** scale with one decimal — use `formatAggregateRating`, not raw stars).

**Common errors:** `to_id_not_exist`, `rating_value_should_be_between_minus_10_and_plus_10`, `to_type_should_be_user_or_community_or_item`, `rating_failed`.

Use **`authFetch`** (`@vtc/client`) or the shell client pattern in posif-svelte — not app-route `Authorization` headers.

---

## `to_type` targets

| `to_type` | `to_id` | Backend checks |
|-----------|---------|----------------|
| `user` | Platform user id | User must exist |
| `community` | Space / group id | Community must exist, not deleted |
| `item` | **Your** stable positive int | No row required — app owns id assignment |

For **app-owned entities** (restaurant, product, article): persist a **`ratingTargetId`** (or equivalent) at create time. API requires an int `to_id`; do not send UUID strings.

**Stable id pattern (Vite apps):** `stableRatingTargetId(seed)` — FNV-style hash into `1 … 2_000_000_000` — see `~/apps/food/src/lib/vtcRatings.ts`. Use one seed per entity (e.g. internal restaurant id) and **never change** it after ratings exist.

