## Slider UX (match the shell)

Canonical UI: **−10 … +10** stepped slider, red → neutral → green track, large numeric readout, Save / Cancel.

| Piece | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Panel component | `~/apps/app/src/lib/components/rating/RatingSliderPanel.svelte` |
| Helpers | `~/apps/app/src/lib/utils/rating-slider.ts` — `coerceSliderRating`, `getRatingSliderBackground`, `formatAggregateRating` |
| API client | `~/apps/app/src/lib/api/people.api.ts` — `addRating`, `getLastRating` |
| Response normalizers | `~/apps/app/src/lib/api/ratings-response.ts` |

**React / Vite child apps:** port the slider markup + helpers (Food Places: `VtcRatingSlider.tsx`, `ratingSlider.ts`) or extract shared UI later — **do not** ship a separate 1–5 star widget for the same platform scores unless product explicitly asks (space About uses the **slider**, not stars).

Display aggregate as **`formatAggregateRating(value)`** (`7.2`, em dash when missing). Filters like “7+” compare against the **aggregate**, not the user’s −10…+10 input.

---

## Integration checklist

1. **Read** aggregate (and optional count) on detail/list — from your entity payload, `GET /ratings/summary`, or denormalized field updated after save.
2. **Write** only when `getAuthToken()` is set; show sign-in copy that matches shell behaviour.
3. **Pre-fill** slider via `GET /ratings/last` before opening the panel.
4. **After save**, refresh aggregate from `POST` `result` or re-fetch summary.
5. **i18n** all labels (`i18n.mdc`) — no hardcoded “Rate this place”.
6. **Do not** duplicate scores in a private Mongo `reviews` collection if ZAPI ratings are the source of truth.

